<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Combat Extended and the gun a dressed quest pawn is handed (CE 16.7.4). The fields are
  QuestPilotExtension's, their rule in the header of Source/1.6/QuestPilot/WeaponAmmo.cs.

  CE gives VFEP's warcasket autorifle a CompAmmoUser with a 30 round magazine of 20x82mm
  (its ModPatches for VFEP, Ranged_Warcaskets.xml) and makes every gun empty: a generated
  pawn's is filled and its spare ammunition put in the inventory by
  LoadoutPropertiesExtension.GenerateLoadoutFor, from CE's postfix on
  PawnWeaponGenerator.TryGenerateWeaponFor, for the gun the pawn holds then. QuestPilot
  exchanges the gun after that, so without these names a dressed pawn's autorifle never fires
  and CE's AI puts it away for fists (CompReload.StartCastChecks).

  ammoComp and ammoLoadMethod: CompAmmoUser.ResetAmmoCount(AmmoDef newAmmo = null), which fills
  the magazine with the gun's first ammunition type, the plain round, when called with null.
  ammoDefProperty and ammoMagazineProperty: CurrentAmmo, an AmmoDef and so a ThingDef, and
  MagSize, an int, for the spare ammunition.
  ammoSpareMagazines 3, the low end of what CE has VFEP's own junkers carry
  (primaryMagazineCount, 3 to 5 for the kinds its PawnKinds_Junkers.xml patches).

  Tests/1.6/CompatPatchTests.cs holds the fields named here to the ones the C# declares.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="HPWC_Warcasket_Hemophage"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="HemophageWarcasket.QuestPilotExtension"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <ammoComp>CombatExtended.CompAmmoUser</ammoComp>
      <ammoLoadMethod>ResetAmmoCount</ammoLoadMethod>
      <ammoDefProperty>CurrentAmmo</ammoDefProperty>
      <ammoMagazineProperty>MagSize</ammoMagazineProperty>
      <ammoSpareMagazines>3</ammoSpareMagazines>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
